from pathlib import Path
import html,json
P=Path
steps=[
('01','Understand the route','An Ingress is a Kubernetes API object containing HTTP host and path routing rules. An ingress controller is the running reverse proxy that watches these objects and handles requests. Creating an Ingress alone does not start a proxy. An IngressClass connects a rule to its controller. Here Traefik handles ingress; NGINX is simply one backend application.', [('Inspect your tools','kubectl config current-context\nkubectl get nodes\nhelm version --short')], [('Why does an Ingress need a controller?','The API stores desired rules; the controller implements them and forwards HTTP requests.'),('Service versus Ingress?','A Service gives selected ready pods a stable network endpoint. Ingress adds HTTP host/path routing in front of Services.')]),
('02','Deploy the controller','Use Docker Desktop with Kubernetes enabled and the docker-desktop context. Allow roughly 3 GB free cluster memory and internet access for image pulls. Run commands in PowerShell from this repository. The vendored official Traefik chart is pinned to 42.2.0. The controller has two replicas, ClusterIP exposure, explicit class traefik, access logs, and native Service load balancing. It does not claim the default IngressClass.', [('Select the local cluster','kubectl config use-context docker-desktop\nkubectl get nodes'),('Install controller','helm upgrade --install lab-ingress ./vendor/traefik-42.2.0.tgz -n ingress-system --create-namespace -f controller-values.yaml --wait --timeout 5m'),('Check controller','kubectl get deployment,pods,svc -n ingress-system\nkubectl get ingressclass traefik')], [('Why two controller replicas?','They demonstrate redundancy, but on this one-node cluster they do not protect against node failure.'),('Why ClusterIP rather than LoadBalancer?','A localhost port-forward provides a predictable local entry point without depending on Docker Desktop external-IP behavior.')]),
('03','Install three application charts','Each small, readable local chart creates a Deployment with two replicas, one ClusterIP Service, and one networking.k8s.io/v1 Ingress. Grafana and Prometheus also receive ConfigMaps. These are educational charts, not the upstream production charts. Use the individual commands below, or scripts/deploy.ps1 to install everything with error checks.', [('Install all applications','helm upgrade --install nginx ./charts/nginx -n ingress-lab --create-namespace --wait --timeout 5m\nhelm upgrade --install prometheus ./charts/prometheus -n ingress-lab --wait --timeout 5m\nhelm upgrade --install grafana ./charts/grafana -n ingress-lab --wait --timeout 5m'),('Inspect the rendered resources','helm template nginx ./charts/nginx -n ingress-lab\nkubectl get deployments,pods,svc,ingress -n ingress-lab\nkubectl get endpointslices -n ingress-lab')], [('How does a Service select pods?','Its selector matches pod labels; EndpointSlices contain the corresponding ready pod addresses.'),('Does two Prometheus replicas mean shared HA storage?','No. Each replica scrapes independently and stores its own temporary data. Requests may hit either replica; this is a routing lab, not a production HA monitoring design.'),('How does Grafana reach Prometheus?','The provisioned datasource uses http://prometheus:9090 inside the namespace, not the external ingress hostname.')]),
('04','Send traffic through ingress','In terminal A, keep the port-forward running. It binds only to localhost and selects one controller pod for this session. In terminal B, send requests with a Host header. No hosts-file changes are needed for curl. Expect HTTP 200 for all three apps and HTTP 404 for an unknown hostname.', [('Terminal A — keep running','kubectl port-forward -n ingress-system svc/lab-ingress-traefik 8080:80 --address 127.0.0.1'),('Terminal B — test all routes','curl.exe -i -H "Host: nginx.lab.test" http://127.0.0.1:8080/\ncurl.exe -i -H "Host: prometheus.lab.test" http://127.0.0.1:8080/-/ready\ncurl.exe -i -H "Host: grafana.lab.test" http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/health\ncurl.exe -i -H "Host: missing.lab.test" http://127.0.0.1:8080/'),('Automated checks','powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/validate.ps1\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/smoke-test.ps1')], [('Why does localhost alone return 404?','The HTTP Host header is localhost, which matches none of the three configured host rules.'),('Does port-forward balance across controller replicas?','No. One port-forward session selects one controller pod. Backend Services still select ready application endpoints; connection reuse can prevent strict alternation.')]),
('05','Open the UIs and observe','For browser access, add the following line to the Windows hosts file at C:\\Windows\\System32\\drivers\\etc\\hosts using an elevated editor, then open the links below while port-forward runs. Browser URLs include port 8080. Grafana permits anonymous Viewer access for this local lab; its Prometheus datasource is already provisioned. Prometheus exposes self metrics and Grafana metrics; stock NGINX does not expose Prometheus metrics.', [('Hosts file entry','127.0.0.1 nginx.lab.test prometheus.lab.test grafana.lab.test'),('Follow the route','kubectl describe ingress nginx -n ingress-lab\nkubectl get svc nginx -n ingress-lab -o wide\nkubectl get endpointslices -n ingress-lab -l kubernetes.io/service-name=nginx -o wide\nkubectl logs -n ingress-system -l app.kubernetes.io/name=traefik --tail=25 --prefix'),('Inspect monitoring','curl.exe -H "Host: prometheus.lab.test" "http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/v1/query?query=up"')], [('What does up equal to 1 mean?','Prometheus successfully scraped that target at its last scrape. It does not prove every app or ingress route is healthy.'),('Why host routing?','Each app keeps its root URL and redirects. Path prefixes would require app base-path configuration or controller-specific rewrites.')]),
('06','Watch recovery and troubleshoot','Delete one NGINX pod using the command below, then watch the Deployment create a replacement. Inspect readiness and EndpointSlices. A fresh request should continue via a ready endpoint, but a single in-flight request can fail during termination; this is not a zero-downtime guarantee. The two pods share one Docker Desktop node.', [('Replace one pod','$pod = kubectl get pod -n ingress-lab -l app=nginx -o jsonpath=\'{.items[0].metadata.name}\'\nkubectl delete pod $pod -n ingress-lab\nkubectl rollout status deployment/nginx -n ingress-lab --timeout=120s\nkubectl get pods -n ingress-lab -l app=nginx'),('Find a failure','kubectl get events -n ingress-lab --sort-by=.lastTimestamp\nkubectl describe pods -n ingress-lab\nkubectl logs deployment/prometheus -n ingress-lab --tail=30')], [('404 versus 503?','404 usually means no matching router/host/path. 503 often means a matched backend has no usable endpoints. Inspect controller logs and EndpointSlices to establish the cause.'),('Pending or ImagePullBackOff?','Pending often indicates scheduling or resource constraints. ImagePullBackOff means the runtime cannot pull the image; inspect events, registry connectivity, and image tags.')]),
('07','Clean up and publish','This lab uses emptyDir storage: pod replacement loses that pod’s Prometheus history and Grafana runtime state. Anonymous Grafana and unauthenticated Prometheus are suitable only for the localhost exercise. Production needs authentication, TLS, durable storage and a real monitoring HA design. Stop port-forward with Ctrl+C. Cleanup uninstalls only this lab’s four releases and retains namespaces.', [('Remove lab releases','powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/cleanup.ps1'),('Create the local Git repository','git init -b main\ngit add .\ngit commit -m "Add tested Kubernetes ingress learning lab"'),('Upload to your own empty GitHub repository','git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/ingress-lab.git\ngit push -u origin main')], [('How would TLS be added?','Use a TLS Secret and spec.tls host configuration, or a certificate manager, and expose an HTTPS entry point with trusted certificates.'),('Ingress versus Gateway API?','Ingress remains usable but its API is frozen. Gateway API offers more expressive routing and role separation; support depends on the chosen controller.')])]
svg='''<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1050 610" role="img" aria-labelledby="title desc"><title id="title">Ingress lab traffic flow</title><desc id="desc">Local HTTP traffic enters one of two Traefik controller pods, follows one of three Ingress host rules to a ClusterIP Service and two ready application pods. Kubernetes API watches are configuration, not traffic.</desc><defs><marker id="a" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="9" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L9,3 L0,6" fill="none" stroke="#287b7b"/></marker></defs><rect width="1050" height="610" rx="20" fill="#f0f8f5"/><style>text{font:16px system-ui;fill:#183d43}.box{fill:white;stroke:#95bcb4;stroke-width:2}.line{stroke:#287b7b;stroke-width:2;fill:none;marker-end:url(#a)}</style><text x="30" y="35" font-weight="bold">DATA PLANE • HTTP requests → host rule → Service → ready pod</text><rect class="box" x="30" y="65" width="260" height="65" rx="12"/><text x="48" y="93">Browser / curl on localhost</text><text x="48" y="116">Host: nginx.lab.test :8080</text><path class="line" d="M290 96 H360"/><rect class="box" x="365" y="65" width="300" height="65" rx="12"/><text x="383" y="93">port-forward → Traefik :80</text><text x="383" y="116">one controller pod per session</text><rect class="box" x="720" y="65" width="290" height="65" rx="12"/><text x="738" y="93">Traefik replica 1 + replica 2</text><text x="738" y="116">Deployment / ingress-system</text><path class="line" d="M515 130 V165 H180 V190"/><path class="line" d="M515 165 V190"/><path class="line" d="M515 165 H850 V190"/>'''
for x,name,port in [(30,'nginx',80),(365,'prometheus',9090),(700,'grafana',3000)]:
 svg+=f'<rect class="box" x="{x}" y="195" width="310" height="70" rx="12"/><text x="{x+18}" y="223">Ingress: {name}.lab.test</text><text x="{x+18}" y="248">Prefix / • class: traefik</text><path class="line" d="M{x+155} 265 V305"/><rect class="box" x="{x}" y="310" width="310" height="60" rx="12"/><text x="{x+18}" y="345">Service: {name}:{port} ClusterIP</text><path class="line" d="M{x+155} 370 V395 H{x+70} V420"/><path class="line" d="M{x+155} 395 H{x+240} V420"/><rect class="box" x="{x}" y="425" width="145" height="55" rx="12"/><rect class="box" x="{x+165}" y="425" width="145" height="55" rx="12"/><text x="{x+18}" y="458">Pod replica 1</text><text x="{x+183}" y="458">Pod replica 2</text>'
svg+='''<text x="30" y="525">CONFIGURATION PLANE • API: Ingress + IngressClass + Services + EndpointSlices → controller watches</text><text x="30" y="555">nativeLBByDefault=true makes Traefik use Service ClusterIPs in this lab.</text><text x="30" y="582">Grafana → prometheus:9090 uses internal DNS. Two replicas on one node are not node-level HA.</text></svg>'''
P('docs/architecture.svg').write_text(svg)
css='''*{box-sizing:border-box}html{scroll-behavior:smooth}body{margin:0;background:#faf9f4;color:#203a42;font:16px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif}header,main,footer{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:32px}header{padding-top:65px}h1{font-size:clamp(38px,6vw,68px);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-3px;max-width:850px}h2{font-size:30px;line-height:1.25}h3{font-size:18px}a{color:#166663}p{max-width:950px}.eyebrow{font-weight:750;letter-spacing:2px;color:#9c5b24}.lead{font-size:21px;max-width:800px}.tags{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px}.tags span{background:#e5f0e9;border-radius:30px;padding:7px 16px}nav{background:#fff;padding:18px;border:1px solid #dce5df;border-radius:16px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px}section{background:white;border:1px solid #dce5df;border-radius:22px;padding:30px;margin:26px 0;scroll-margin-top:20px}.number{color:#bd6c36;font-size:17px;display:block;letter-spacing:2px}.code{position:relative;background:#eff5f4;border:1px solid #d3e2de;border-radius:12px;margin:14px 0}pre{overflow:auto;padding:48px 20px 20px;margin:0;white-space:pre;font:14px/1.7 Consolas,monospace;color:#163d43}button{position:absolute;right:10px;top:10px;background:#fff;color:#245a56;border:1px solid #b9d0c9;border-radius:7px;padding:5px 12px;cursor:pointer}button:focus-visible,a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #cb7d36;outline-offset:3px}details{border-top:1px solid #e3eae5;padding:13px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:650}.note{background:#fff1d9;border-left:4px solid #d59c47;padding:18px;border-radius:6px}img{width:100%;height:auto}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}td,th{text-align:left;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #dde6e1}footer{color:#56706f}@media(max-width:600px){header,main,footer{padding:18px}section{padding:20px}h1{letter-spacing:-1px}}@media print{button,nav{display:none}section{break-inside:avoid}pre{white-space:pre-wrap}body{background:white}}'''
parts=['<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Ingress, understood • A hands-on Kubernetes lab</title><style>'+css+'</style><header><div class="eyebrow">KUBERNETES / LEARN BY ROUTING</div><h1>One entry point.<br>Three applications.<br>Every hop explained.</h1><p class="lead">A practical Docker Desktop lab for understanding ingress traffic with Grafana, Prometheus and NGINX.</p><div class="tags"><span>7 guided labs</span><span>2 replicas per app</span><span>Helm + PowerShell</span><span>Offline-friendly guide</span></div></header><main><nav aria-label="Lab sections">']
parts += [f'<a href="#lab{n}">{n} {title}</a>' for n,title,*_ in steps]
parts+=['</nav><section><h2>Continue learning</h2><p><a href="lab2-argocd.html">Section 2: Argo CD and GitOps labs →</a></p></section><section><h2>Your traffic map</h2><img src="docs/architecture.svg" alt="Traffic diagram showing localhost to Traefik, three host routes, three Services and two pods per application."><p>Solid arrows show the request path. Ingress rules configure the controller; they are not separate running proxies. Services map to ready endpoints, not a fixed alternating pod sequence.</p><div class="note">The retired community ingress-nginx controller is not used. Traefik is the controller; the NGINX web server is an application. All access is local HTTP for learning.</div></section><section><h2>What you will deploy</h2><table><tr><th>Host</th><th>Service port</th><th>Replicas</th><th>Purpose</th></tr><tr><td>nginx.lab.test</td><td>80</td><td>2</td><td>Simple web backend</td></tr><tr><td>prometheus.lab.test</td><td>9090</td><td>2</td><td>Independent metric collectors</td></tr><tr><td>grafana.lab.test</td><td>3000</td><td>2</td><td>Provisioned metrics explorer</td></tr></table><p>Repository contents: charts/ contains the three application charts; vendor/ contains the official controller chart; controller-values.yaml configures it; scripts/ deploys, validates, tests and cleans up. <a href="docs/TEST-RESULTS.md">Read the actual local test report</a>.</p></section>']
for n,title,body,commands,qa in steps:
 parts.append(f'<section id="lab{n}"><span class="number">LAB {n}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{html.escape(body)}</p>')
 for label,cmd in commands:parts.append('<h3>'+label+'</h3><div class="code"><button type="button" aria-label="Copy '+html.escape(label)+'">Copy</button><pre><code>'+html.escape(cmd)+'</code></pre></div>')
 if n=='05':parts.append('<p>Open: <a href="http://nginx.lab.test:8080">NGINX</a> · <a href="http://prometheus.lab.test:8080">Prometheus</a> · <a href="http://grafana.lab.test:8080/explore">Grafana Explore</a>. Select Prometheus and query <code>up</code>. Wait about 30 seconds for initial scrapes.</p>')
 parts.append('<h3>Interview questions &amp; answers</h3><p>Review these answers after completing this lab. Click a question to collapse its answer for self-testing.</p>')
 for q,a in qa:parts.append('<details class="interview" open><summary>'+html.escape(q)+'</summary><p><strong>Answer:</strong> '+html.escape(a)+'</p></details>')
 parts.append('</section>')
parts.append('<section><h2>Explore every chart file</h2><p>Expand a file to inspect and copy the exact repository source. Change values.yaml, then repeat helm upgrade --install to apply your change.</p>')
for path in [P('controller-values.yaml'),*sorted(P('charts').rglob('*.yaml'))]:parts.append('<details><summary>'+str(path).replace('\\','/')+'</summary><div class="code"><button type="button">Copy</button><pre><code>'+html.escape(path.read_text())+'</code></pre></div></details>')
parts.append('''</section><section><h2>References</h2><p><a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/ingress/">Kubernetes Ingress</a> · <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/service/">Services</a> · <a href="https://doc.traefik.io/traefik/reference/install-configuration/providers/kubernetes/kubernetes-ingress/">Traefik Ingress provider</a> · <a href="https://github.com/traefik/traefik-helm-chart">Official Traefik chart</a> · <a href="https://kubernetes.io/blog/2025/11/11/ingress-nginx-retirement/">ingress-nginx retirement</a></p></section></main><footer>Built for learning • localhost HTTP • Docker Desktop Kubernetes • Open index.html directly, no build or CDN required.<span id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></footer><script>document.querySelectorAll('.code button').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',async()=>{const t=b.parentElement.querySelector('code').textContent;try{if(navigator.clipboard&&window.isSecureContext){await navigator.clipboard.writeText(t)}else{const a=document.createElement('textarea');a.value=t;a.style.position='fixed';a.style.opacity='0';document.body.append(a);a.select();if(!document.execCommand('copy'))throw Error('copy');a.remove()}b.textContent='Copied!';document.getElementById('status').textContent='Command copied';setTimeout(()=>b.textContent='Copy',1800)}catch(e){b.textContent='Select text to copy';document.getElementById('status').textContent='Clipboard unavailable. Select the command and press Ctrl+C.'}}));</script></html>''')
P('index.html').write_text(''.join(parts),encoding='utf-8')
P('README.md').write_text('''# Ingress, understood

Open **index.html** for the full light-themed guide, diagram, copy buttons, all chart sources, and interview checkpoints after each lab. No frontend installation required.

## Quick start (PowerShell)

Docker Desktop Kubernetes must be enabled. You need kubectl, Helm 3 or 4, registry internet access, and the docker-desktop context. Run from the repository root:

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/deploy.ps1
kubectl port-forward -n ingress-system svc/lab-ingress-traefik 8080:80 --address 127.0.0.1
```

In a second terminal:

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/validate.ps1
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/smoke-test.ps1
```

Use the HTML guide for hosts-file/browser instructions, manual installation, traffic flow, troubleshooting and cleanup.

## Scope

Three locally authored Helm charts: nginx, prometheus, grafana. Each has two replicas and a ClusterIP Service and host-based Ingress. Official Traefik chart 42.2.0 is vendored under vendor/. Grafana datasource is provisioned. Prometheus scrapes itself and Grafana. NGINX has no metrics exporter. Two independent Prometheus instances and ephemeral Grafana state are deliberate learning simplifications, not production HA. HTTP and anonymous Grafana are restricted to a localhost exercise. All images and controller chart are pinned by version tag, not immutable digest.

[Actual test evidence](docs/TEST-RESULTS.md) · [Traffic diagram](docs/architecture.svg)

## GitHub

This is a local Git repository; create an empty repository in your GitHub account, then set its URL and push. No GitHub upload is performed automatically. See the HTML guide for commands. The vendored upstream chart retains its upstream license. Your application charts and guide use the MIT license.
''')
